12
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:46,000
The poinsettia (; Euphorbia pulcherrima) is a commercially important
flowering plant species of the diverse spurge family Euphorbiaceae.

13
00:41:53,333 --> 00:41:59,333
Indigenous to Mexico and Central America, the poinsettia
was first described by Europeans in 1834.

14
00:45:06,666 --> 00:45:12,666
It is particularly well known for its red and green foliage and
is widely used in Christmas floral displays.

15
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:26,000
It derives its common English name from Joel Roberts Poinsett, the first United States minister to Mexico, who is credited with introducing the plant to the US in the 1820s;
however, there have been recent efforts to rename the flower to its Nahuatl name, "cuetlaxōchitl", due to Poinsett's involvement in slavery and the Trail of Tears.

16
00:51:33,333 --> 00:51:39,333
Poinsettias are shrubs or small trees, with
heights of 0.6 to 4 m (2.0 to 13.1 ft).

17
00:54:46,666 --> 00:54:52,666
Though often stated to be highly toxic, the poinsettia
is not dangerous to pets or children.

18
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Exposure to the plant, even consumption, most often results in no
effect, though it can cause nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea.

19
01:01:13,333 --> 01:01:19,333
Wild poinsettias occur from Mexico to southern Guatemala,
growing on mid-elevation, Pacific-facing slopes.

20
01:04:26,666 --> 01:04:32,666
One population in the Mexican state of Guerrero is much further inland, however,
and is thought to be the ancestor of most cultivated populations.

21
01:07:40,000 --> 01:07:46,000
Wild poinsettia populations are highly fragmented, as their habitat
is experiencing largely unregulated deforestation.

22
01:10:53,333 --> 01:10:59,333
They were cultivated by the Aztecs for use in traditional medicine.

23
01:14:06,666 --> 01:14:12,666
They became associated with the Christmas holiday
and are popular seasonal decorations.

24
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:26,000
Every year in the United States, approximately 70 million poinsettias of
many cultivated varieties are sold in a six-week period.

25
01:20:33,333 --> 01:20:39,333
Many of these poinsettias are grown by Paul Ecke Ranch, which serves
half the worldwide market and 70 percent of the US market.

26
01:23:46,666 --> 01:23:52,666
The tone is emotional.
